===Results===
Despite trailing in most polling, Jim Hodges was decisively elected. Unsurprisingly, Hodges performed extremely well in the rural counties, but it was the unexpectedly strong vote of the [[South Carolina Low Country|Lowcountry]] in his favor that enabled Hodges to defeat Beasley. [[Voter turnout]] decreased dramatically versus the [[South Carolina gubernatorial election, 1994|previous election]] because approximately 500 thousand new voters were added to the rolls, but many of those chose not to vote in the election.

